    {
      "title": "Trump says US to send one-time $90 payment to 20m seniors enrolled in Medicare",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/03/trump-payment-seniors-medicare",
      "description": "<p>President says payments, to be sent in early October, are meant to offset cost of monthly insurance premiums</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump\">Donald ⁠Trump</a> has said the US government will send a one-time $90 payment to more than 20 million Americans enrolled in <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/medicare\">Medicare</a>, the ⁠health insurance program for ⁠elderly people, ​to help offset the cost of their monthly medical insurance premiums.</p><p>The president said on social media late on Friday that the ⁠payments would come from the Medicare Improvement Fund, which he said was given $2bn by <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-congress\">Congress</a> to improve the Medicare fee-for-service program.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/03/trump-payment-seniors-medicare\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-03T13:48:21"
    }
